    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0534" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg454"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. White reports that he has applied in behalf of the Eisemanns for an
                    extension of leave to remain in Frankfort until April, 1903; <pb facs="0535"
                        n="455" xml:id="pg455"/> that the brother at present in Germany declares
                    that they will then be ready to return to Boston.</p>
                <p>Mr. White has stated very fully to the foreign office the reasons for this
                    request.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
